 ## Account store
 
 Phase 3 store-managed accounts and the three-way `shunt login claude` flow are implemented. Each login writes one Claude Code-compatible JSON file under `~/.shunt/accounts/claude/`. Name-only entries select those files explicitly; an empty configured account list scans the directory. Full-OAuth and imported logins retain a refresh token and are refreshed through the existing `ClaudeAuthStore`; setup-token accounts are static until their one-year token expires or receives a 401. The optional M9 admin surface can provision full-OAuth or setup-token accounts through a manual-paste browser flow; importing an existing host credential remains CLI-only.
+
+## Organization scope
+
+When `organization_uuid` is present, pool identity is the pair of Anthropic user UUID and organization UUID. Personal and Team subscriptions for the same user then keep separate quotas, cooldowns, pauses, relogin state, refresh locks, and subscription-plan caches. Aliases for the same pair still share state. Store-managed accounts read `shuntOrganizationUuid`; OAuth provisioning saves it when the token exchange returns an organization. Existing accounts without this metadata retain their previous identity. The raw user `uuid` remains the value sent in `metadata.user_id.account_uuid`.
+
+The local `x-shunt-session-account` request header prefers a configured account name for a Claude OAuth Messages request. It only reorders eligible accounts: pauses, hard caps, quota thresholds, and reactive failover still apply. Shunt consumes the header and never sends it upstream.
+
+Aggregate `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-status: rejected` also triggers quota rotation. When `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-representative-claim` identifies `five_hour`, `seven_day`, or `seven_day_oi`, its status and `anthropic-ratelimit-unified-reset` are recorded for that window without inventing utilization. A null polling reading does not clear an unexpired rejection. The aggregate expires at its own reported reset (or the existing bounded lifetime when absent). `overage-status: rejected` alone never exhausts subscription quota. Admin account snapshots expose `status_5h`, `status_7d`, and `status_7d_oi` separately from percentages. Exhausted-pool errors retain the last attempted account name in `x-shunt-account`.
+
+When admission skips a busy identity and the remaining candidates only report quota rejection, the pool returns a retryable `503 api_error` with `retry-after: 1`, rather than presenting the last account's weekly limit as pool-wide exhaustion.
