 unaffected: the router takes only its own id out of that prefix's reach.
+
+### Organization scope
+
+When `organization_uuid` is present, pool identity is the pair of Anthropic user UUID and organization UUID. Personal and Team subscriptions for the same user then keep separate quotas, cooldowns, pauses, relogin state, and refresh locks. Aliases for the same pair still share state. Store-managed accounts read `shuntOrganizationUuid`; OAuth provisioning saves it when the token exchange returns an organization. Existing accounts without this metadata retain their previous identity. The raw user `uuid` remains the value sent in `metadata.user_id.account_uuid`.
+
+The local `x-shunt-session-account` request header prefers a configured account name for a Claude OAuth Messages request. It only reorders eligible accounts: pauses, hard caps, quota thresholds, and reactive failover still apply. Shunt consumes the header and never sends it upstream.
